# Vietnamese bound-phrase emphasis

Vietnamese compound words are often two syllables (`im lặng`, `hình ảnh`). They are listed in `VIETNAMESE_BOUND_PHRASES` in `features/kinetic-text/lib/text-language.ts`.

**Never emphasize only part of a bound phrase.** If scoring picks one syllable, call `expandEmphasisToBoundPhrases` so every syllable in that phrase is emphasized together.

When adding new two-syllable Vietnamese words, add both accented and unaccented forms to `VIETNAMESE_BOUND_PHRASES`.

Bad: only `lặng` glows in `… im lặng.`

Good: both `im` and `lặng` glow together with the **same** emphasis variant (halo, sweep, etc.) — use `getBoundPhraseEmphasisSeed` / `getBoundPhraseStartIndex`, not per-syllable variant keys.

Emphasis must not create oversized spaces. Phrase containers retain intrinsic width and use a single `0.24em` gap, including inside shared frames. Never center a full-width highlighted phrase beside other words in a non-wrapping line. Look up emphasis with each word's original page index, not its segment-local position.
